import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data consumer_relies_on_incidental_realization_property: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "consumer_relies_on_incidental_realization_property" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a consumer relies on a property of its provider's current implementation that the provider's contract does not promise. DISTINGUISHING FACT, the class that recurs: OwnerOnly's O_EXCL is incidental to MODE, not its contract. Complete exclusive publication is WriteCreateNew, published via extdeps.filesystem.rust_realization (complete content then hard_link). A consumer that treats OwnerOnly as exclusive complete publication is leaning on a disclaimed property; the next instance need not be a CAS writer. HARM: a contract-preserving provider change can invalidate the consumer, and even the current implementation may establish only part of the property the consumer assumes. Agreement on happy-path output conceals the missing guarantee; reviewing the implementation alone cannot repair the dependency contract.",

    "SPECIMEN, REPAIRED AT THE REALIZATION HOME (silent-stag-307): gunbc.durable_cas_file_store cas_commit_at previously used Filesystem.WriteOwnerOnly, whose v1 interpreter realization opens the FINAL path then write_all. cas_commit_at now publishes through Filesystem.WriteCreateNew. WriteOwnerOnly remains the owner-only MODE operation. This receipt records that repair; it does not redefine the class as 'CAS now uses WriteCreateNew'.",

    "EXECUTED on BuildBuddy amd64: cargo test --release -p v1-compiler --lib write_file_create_new (11 tests), covering a_write_failure_after_creation_leaves_no_target_behind and direct_final_path_open_then_write_leaves_a_target_when_the_write_fails.",

    "NOT YET EXECUTED, receipt owed: the four test.claim.durable_cas_file_store_wet_witness identities, which are the only cells that run file_compare_and_set against a real filesystem. They are enrolled on the local-repo wet lane and route-gapped out of the hermetic floor (v2.workflow.floor_route_gap floor_route_gap_expectation_chunk_11), so floor green is silent about them by construction. This row does not treat those names as executed evidence.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT BY EXECUTION: mechanically preventable for exclusive complete VISIBILITY of a generation file, at the grain of the rust write_file_create_new suite and no higher. Crash-durable directory metadata is NOT claimed: rust_realization fsyncs the staging file and does not fsync the parent directory after hard_link.",

    "CEILING: structurally guaranteed for the internal bind of CAS to WriteCreateNew once acceptance refuses a consumer of WriteOwnerOnly for exclusive complete publication; external crash durability remains outside the modeled guarantee. NEXT TRIGGER for composition: an executed receipt of the four wet identities on the local-repo wet lane. NEXT TRIGGER for crash-durable directory metadata: a publication contract that includes parent-directory sync, with executed evidence, or acceptance that refuses WriteOwnerOnly as a CAS publication primitive.",

    "DISPOSITION: production CAS publication uses WriteCreateNew. The discriminating RED and the retired-construction mutation control stay enrolled (DESIGN 4b(4)). gunbc.fabric_control_plane still consumes file_compare_and_set; successful CellReserved and race ReservationLost are unchanged in meaning. Torn generations at the slot path are no longer a WriteOwnerOnly leftover wearing a commit.",

    "CONSUMPTION: this per-class record joins the derived gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.roster recurring_failure_mode_roster.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.durable_cas_file_store", decl_name: "cas_commit_at"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.durable_cas_file_store", decl_name: "cas_outcome_from_create"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "extdeps.filesystem.rust_realization", decl_name: "rust_file_write_create_new_fn_def"),
  ],
